PRETABLE 4 -- #531, kill table 4: THE VERIFYING PASS the fable5 adjudication pre-committed.
Written 2026-09-18 BEFORE table 4 runs; this file's mtime is the order discriminator.
PRETABLE{,2,3}.out are NOT edited -- their mtimes are the order proofs for tables 1-3.

================================================================================
WHAT THIS PASS IS FOR, AND WHAT WOULD CLOSE THE CHAIN
================================================================================
The fable5 ruling pre-committed the stop condition, and it is a FORK, not a hope:

  * this pass confirms ZERO cells OUTSIDE the stated enumeration, denominator named
      -> only already-enumerated cells, now killed        => THE CHAIN CLOSES
  * a mutant escapes that is OUTSIDE the enumeration
      -> the fresh-process-probe-versus-shared-lifetime-latch ARCHITECTURE is the
         root cause, and the latch axis drops WHOLESALE to disclosed debt rather
         than being chased into pass six

So this table's job is VERIFICATION, not search.  It re-builds the cells opus5 measured
as escapes and asks whether the closure now kills them.

================================================================================
1. THE ENUMERATION, AND WHY IT SHRANK FROM 14 TO 10
================================================================================
{announce sites} x {announce fires, latch sets} + {2 collision directions}

The F13 SILENT-DECLINE repair removed the two READ-arm announces, so the announce sites
went 6 -> 4 and the space went 14 -> 10 cells.  *Resolving a design question removed four
cells of detector work rather than adding them.*

*** TWO OF opus5's EIGHT MUTANTS ARE NOW INAPPLICABLE, NOT UNTESTED: MF_nolatchset28rd and
the 0x10020-READ latch-set MUTATE STATEMENTS THAT NO LONGER EXIST. ***  The mutator treats
MUTANT-TEXT-NOT-FOUND as a HARD FAIL, so an inapplicable mutant is loud rather than a
silent no-op.  Four latch-set statements survive and all four are mutated below.

================================================================================
2. CHANNEL -- per mutant, the row that must kill it, and the PREDICTION
================================================================================
  MUTANT            CELL                          ROW THAT MUST RED       PREDICT
  V1_assign20wr     collision ISR->TICK (opus MA) xbit rev                KILL 31/32
  V2_assigntick     collision TICK->ISR (opus MD) xbit isr                KILL 31/32
  V3_nolatch20wr    latch-set 0x10020-WR (MB)     latch 1x                KILL 31/32
  V4_nolatch28wr    latch-set 0x10028-WR          latch 28wr              KILL 31/32
  V5_nolatch30wr    latch-set 0x10030-WR (MG)     latch 30wr              KILL 31/32
  V6_nolatchtick    latch-set TICK (opus ME)      latch tick              KILL 31/32
  V7_nocounter      counter liveness (opus MH)    -- none --              ESCAPE 32/32
  V8_len4           width axis (opus MC)          -- none --              ESCAPE 32/32

*** THE LAST TWO ARE PREDICTED TO ESCAPE AND THAT IS NOT A BREACH. ***  Both are DISCLOSED
debt with a ruling behind them:
  * V7: fable5 measured the counter increment UNCONDITIONAL, two lines ABOVE the guard the
    fix de-fatalised -- so it is PRE-EXISTING, FIX-INDEPENDENT behaviour, coverage debt and
    not a clause-(d) cell.  The de-escalation accept side IS pinned, by `tick 50' +
    `tick 50 txt'.
  * V8: the body never tests `len', so by the pcc2widthkills bound it is a single-operand
    marginal -- clause (e), not floor.  opus5 noted the cost is low and the reason (e)
    normally excuses value-domains is absent here; it is carried as CHEAP DEBT with that
    cost named, not silently.

*** IF EITHER OF THOSE TWO KILLS ANYWAY, THAT IS A RESULT, NOT A BONUS: it would mean a row
observes something its own comment does not claim, and the row owes a re-reading. ***

================================================================================
3. WHAT WOULD FALSIFY THE CLOSURE
================================================================================
Any of V1..V6 scoring 32/32.  Each names exactly one row that must red; if the named row
stays green the cell is still open and the closure's claim is false at that cell.

AND THE HONEST LIMIT ON WHAT A CLEAN TABLE HERE PROVES: it verifies the ENUMERATION, not
the absence of cells nobody enumerated.  That is precisely why the fable5 fork exists -- a
clean table closes the chain, and an escape OUTSIDE these ten cells does NOT buy pass six.
